Package: notepad-plus-plus-gtk
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: adwaita-icon-theme, fonts-dejavu-core, librsvg2-common, libvte-2.91-0,
            openssh-client, libenchant-2-2, hunspell-en-us | hunspell-dictionary
Description: Notepad++ source code editor - native GTK 3 port (preview)
 Unofficial native Linux build of the Notepad++ source tree using the GTK 3
 backend of Scintilla. This preview provides tabbed editing in two views,
 syntax highlighting for all Notepad++ languages via Lexilla and User Defined
 Languages, Notepad++ colour themes and the Style Configurator, encoding
 detection, the Find / Replace / Find in Files / Mark dialog with Boost
 regex and a search results panel, macros, Run commands, the Shortcut Mapper,
 Preferences, Notepad++ translations, printing, docking panels (Function
 List, Folder as Workspace, Document Map, Project Panels, a terminal and
 others),
 sessions with snapshots of
 unsaved documents, recent files, detection of outside file changes, and a
 single-instance mode compatible with Notepad++ switches. Notepad++'s
 shortcuts.xml, stylers.xml, themes and userDefineLang.xml work unchanged.
 .
 Plugins use Notepad++'s plugin interface, rebuilt for Linux with the SDK in
 notepad-plus-plus-gtk-dev. The bundled Remote Files plugin edits files on FTP
 and SFTP servers, or over an ssh shell link (both through openssh-client). The
 bundled Spell Checker underlines misspellings as you type, with Enchant's
 Hunspell or Aspell dictionaries. Auto-completion, smart
 highlighting and the other Preferences work as in Notepad++.

Package: notepad-plus-plus-gtk-dev
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libgtk-3-dev, ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: notepad-plus-plus-gtk
Description: Notepad++ source code editor - GTK 3 port, plugin SDK
 Headers and a pkg-config file (notepad-plus-plus-gtk-plugin) to build
 plugins for notepad-plus-plus-gtk: Notepad++'s own plugin interface
 (PluginInterface.h, Notepad_plus_msgs.h, Docking.h, menuCmdID.h and
 Scintilla.h, unchanged) on a small windows.h that provides the Win32 types
 and SendMessage. Plugins keep their source, messages and notifications and
 build their user interface with GTK. A sample plugin is included.
